   \textbackslash{}usepackage\{upgreek\}
   \textbackslash{}setlength\{\textbackslash{}oddsidemargin\}\{-69pt\}
   \textbackslash{}begin\{document\}\$\$3+1\$\$\textbackslash{}end\{documen
   t\}D radar point cloud clustering methodology tailored for smart
   infrastructure-based perception applications. This approach first
   performs semantic segmentation of the radar point cloud, followed by
   instance segmentation to generate well-formed clusters with class labels
   using a deep neural network. It also detects single-point objects that
   conventional methods often miss. The described approach is developed and
   experimented using a smart infrastructure-based sensor setup and it
   performs segmentation of the point cloud in real-time. Experimental
   results demonstrate 95.35\% F1-macro score for semantic segmentation and
   91.03\% mean average precision (mAP) at an intersection over union (IoU)
   threshold of 0.5 for instance segmentation. Further, the complete
   pipeline operates at 43.61 frames per second with a memory requirement
   of less than 0.7 MB on the edge device (Nvidia Jetson AGX Orin). We will
   release the RoadsideRadar dataset along with the code implementation of
   this work at https://github.com/bhanderisavan/roadside-radar-seg.},
